-- The other limit (overnight card O6, 2026-10-11): a rule declared in a WHERE is
-- local and is named bare, so two locals of one name give a single entry. The
-- rows answer 30, 50 and 80, and every one lists `WITH scaled: rate`.

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
useOne MEANS scaled WITH base IS n
  WHERE
    GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 3
          base IS A NUMBER
    GIVETH A NUMBER
    scaled MEANS rate TIMES base

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
useTwo MEANS scaled WITH base IS n
  WHERE
    GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 5
          base IS A NUMBER
    GIVETH A NUMBER
    scaled MEANS rate TIMES base

@export default Combine
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      one IS A BOOLEAN
      two IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE combine IS (IF one THEN useOne n ELSE 0) PLUS (IF two THEN useTwo n ELSE 0)
